# Auth & Authorization Rules

## Authentication

- **Laravel Breeze** with Inertia/React stack
- **Sanctum** for session-based auth
- Email verification required (`MustVerifyEmail` on User model)
- Auth controllers in `app/Http/Controllers/Auth/`
- Auth routes in `routes/auth.php`

## Authorization — Policies

Policies are the primary auth mechanism. Located in `app/Policies/`.

### Instance Admin Bypass
```php
// In AppServiceProvider boot()
Gate::before(function ($user, $ability) {
    if ($user->isInstanceAdmin()) return true;
});
```
Instance admins bypass ALL policy checks.

### Policy Registration
Policies are auto-discovered by Laravel convention:
- `WorkspacePolicy` → `Workspace` model
- `ProjectPolicy` → `Project` model
- etc.

### Policy Check in Controllers
```php
$this->authorize('update', $workspace);
$this->authorize('create', [Board::class, $project]);
```

### Role Hierarchy
```
Workspace: owner > admin > editor > viewer/member
Project:   admin > editor > viewer
Bookmark:  creator > editor > viewer
```

### Role Helpers on User Model
```php
$user->workspaceRole($workspace);  // returns role string
$user->projectRole($project);
$user->hasWorkspaceAccess($workspace);
$user->hasProjectAccess($project);
$user->isInstanceAdmin();
```

### Common Policy Pattern
```php
public function update(User $user, Workspace $workspace): bool
{
    $role = $user->workspaceRole($workspace);
    return in_array($role, ['owner', 'admin']);
}
```

## Middleware

- `auth` — Laravel built-in session auth
- `verified` — Email must be verified
- `HandleInertiaRequests` — Shares global data to all pages:
  - `auth.user` — Current user
  - `flash` — Flash messages
  - `workspaces` — User's workspace list
  - `currentWorkspace` — Active workspace with full project/board/page tree
  - `currentPageUuid` — Currently viewed page UUID

## Route Protection
```php
// Public (no auth)
Route::get('/', fn() => Inertia::render('Welcome'));

// Auth + Verified
Route::middleware(['auth', 'verified'])->group(function () {
    // All app routes here
});
```

## Spatie Permissions

- Package: `spatie/laravel-permission` v6
- `HasRoles` trait on User model
- Permission tables created via Spatie migration
- Used alongside custom role logic on workspace/project pivots
